Local engine.py patches (2026-10-19): tap jitter tolerance, 350 ms tap window,
distance-based pointer start, fresh subpixel state, and report-rate-independent gain.
GTK source-event intervals optionally drive velocity; lifetime timing stays monotonic.
Multi-finger gestures stay latched until every contact lifts: a trailing finger
cannot move the pointer or start a glide. Two-to-one transitions clear pointer
origin/velocity; duration, cumulative travel, established pointer intent and max
finger count remain unchanged so real two-finger taps still right-click without
reclassifying an earlier pointer movement as a tap.
